{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01YbTdXQPucbNhmZBSgm4n4y","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"```yaml\ntiers:\n  best:\n    meaning: \"15-model scaling + all planned experiments confirm and strengthen v5 framing; η_max dominance survives every robustness check; GAM 6:6 split validated with bootstrapped CIs; new experiments add independent evidence lines\"\n    key_assumptions:\n      - \"plan_001 scaling to 15 models succeeds (DONE) AND remaining planned experiments (plan_003 RF contrast, plan_009 VIF, plan_010 aggregation expansion) produce consistent results\"\n      - \"Wild cluster bootstrap η_max stays ≥5/12; clustered SE η_max stays ≥8/12\"\n      - \"K_eff fragility confirmed: bootstrap ≤1/12, clustered SE ≤1/12 — clean separation from η_max\"\n      - \"GAM 6:6 split survives bootstrapped CIs at ≥5/6 conditions per attack category\"\n      - \"Random-fault experiment (plan_003) shows K_eff significant ≥2/2 — BFT contrast holds\"\n      - \"Capability-matched validation (plan_004) shows K_eff emerges when η_max variance controlled\"\n      - \"Aggregation gradient replicates under clustered SE: Bayesian still flips K_eff direction\"\n      - \"No reviewer-blocking multicollinearity issue (VIF < 5 after residualization)\"\n    number_ranges:\n      eta_max_sig_bootstrap: [5, 8]\n      eta_max_sig_clustered_se: [8, 11]\n      keff_sig_bootstrap: [0, 1]\n      keff_sig_clustered_se: [0, 1]\n      eta_keff_dominance_ratio_bootstrap: [5, 11]\n      gam_keff_split_targeted_positive: [5, 6]\n      gam_keff_split_sharedbias_negative: [5, 6]\n      rf_keff_sig: [2, 2]\n      rf_r2: [0.70, 0.85]\n      min_eta_max_wins: [12, 12]\n      bayesian_keff_negative_frac: [5, 7]\n      practical_delta_asr_keff_iqr_pp: [0.5, 2.0]\n      diversity_capability_r: [0.65, 0.75]\n    narrative_direction: \"Original framing fully sustained. Title 1/2 work as-is. Five-contribution stack intact: (1) η_max dominance with 5:1+ ratio is the headline; (2) K_eff fragility is a clean null — diversity doesn't independently matter after correcting for non-independence; (3) GAM 6:6 split is a validated mechanistic taxonomy; (4) RF contrast provides the BFT reversal evidence; (5) Aggregation gradient is a prescriptive lever. Methodological transparency section becomes a strength, not a hedge. Paper reads as a confident empirical contribution with actionable defense recommendations.\"\n\n  median:\n    meaning: \"Current evidence (plan001_step1_full_v4) is essentially what we ship; remaining experiments add marginal support or reveal minor inconsistencies that require softened claims but no structural reframe\"\n    key_assumptions:\n      - \"No additional experiments beyond what's already DONE produce strong new evidence (remaining planned experiments either not run due to time/compute, or results are mixed)\"\n      - \"Bootstrap η_max stays at 5/12 (lower bound); no improvement from additional analysis\"\n      - \"K_eff bootstrap stays at 1/12 but clustered SE gives 0/12 — separation exists but is method-dependent\"\n      - \"GAM 6:6 split holds qualitatively but bootstrapped CIs show 2-3 conditions per category are NS — pattern directional, not individually robust\"\n      - \"RF contrast (plan_003) either not completed or shows K_eff sig 1/2 — partial BFT support\"\n      - \"VIF analysis reveals moderate multicollinearity (VIF 3-5) requiring additional discussion but not invalidating results\"\n      - \"Aggregation gradient holds under OLS but Bayesian K_eff flip partially attenuated under clustered SE (3-4/7 negative instead of 6/7)\"\n      - \"arc benchmark consistently weaker than MMLU (η_max 1/6 vs 4/6 under bootstrap) — benchmark asymmetry needs explicit discussion\"\n    number_ranges:\n      eta_max_sig_bootstrap: [4, 6]\n      eta_max_sig_clustered_se: [6, 8]\n      keff_sig_bootstrap: [0, 2]\n      keff_sig_clustered_se: [0, 2]\n      eta_keff_dominance_ratio_bootstrap: [3, 5]\n      gam_keff_split_targeted_positive: [4, 6]\n      gam_keff_split_sharedbias_negative: [3, 5]\n      rf_keff_sig: [1, 2]\n      rf_r2: [0.55, 0.75]\n      min_eta_max_wins: [10, 12]\n      bayesian_keff_negative_frac: [3, 5]\n      practical_delta_asr_keff_iqr_pp: [0.5, 2.5]\n      diversity_capability_r: [0.60, 0.75]\n    narrative_direction: \"Claims require hedging but core story survives. η_max dominance downgraded from 'robust' to 'directional with benchmark-dependent strength' — MMLU strong, ARC weak, must discuss why. K_eff fragility still holds but framed as 'inconclusive' rather than 'clean null'. GAM 6:6 split presented as 'suggestive taxonomic pattern warranting further investigation' rather than confirmed mechanism. RF contrast becomes a partial validation (if completed) or acknowledged limitation (if not). Aggregation gradient retains OLS results with caveat that clustered SE validation is incomplete. Paper shifts from 5-contribution to 3-contribution focus: (1) η_max dominance (primary), (2) methodological transparency on non-independence (elevated to co-primary — the correction story itself becomes a contribution), (3) practical defense recommendations (min_eta_max still wins). Title softened to candidate 2 or 3. 'Diversity Trap' title likely too strong — 'Weakest Link' framing preferred. Supplementary materials carry more analytical weight to address reviewer concerns about incomplete robustness checks.\"\n\n  worst:\n    meaning: \"Additional experiments or deeper analysis reveal that η_max dominance is substantially a statistical artifact of benchmark/model selection; core framing collapses but the dataset and methodological insights remain publishable under a different angle\"\n    key_assumptions:\n      - \"Bootstrap η_max drops below 4/12 (e.g., position 0 imbalance issue generalizes — cluster imbalance inflates significance across positions)\"\n      - \"VIF analysis reveals severe multicollinearity (VIF > 5-10): η_max and K_eff cannot be reliably separated in this design\"\n      - \"RF contrast fails: K_eff not significant even under random faults (plan_003 GO/NO-GO gate fails) — BFT framing collapses entirely\"\n      - \"GAM 6:6 split breaks under corrected inference: actual pattern is 3-4/6 per category with 2+ reversals — no clean mechanistic taxonomy\"\n      - \"Aggregation gradient substantially attenuated: Bayesian K_eff flip disappears under clustered SE (0-1/7 negative)\"\n      - \"ARC benchmark results almost entirely NS under any correction — effectively a single-benchmark study (MMLU only)\"\n      - \"Capability-matched analysis (plan_004) shows η_max significance disappears when capability range is restricted — dominance was driven by capability tier spread, not a general principle\"\n      - \"A competing paper appears demonstrating diversity benefits for LLM judge panels under more realistic threat models\"\n    number_ranges:\n      eta_max_sig_bootstrap: [2, 4]\n      eta_max_sig_clustered_se: [4, 6]\n      keff_sig_bootstrap: [0, 2]\n      keff_sig_clustered_se: [0, 1]\n      eta_keff_dominance_ratio_bootstrap: [1, 3]\n      gam_keff_split_targeted_positive: [2, 4]\n      gam_keff_split_sharedbias_negative: [2, 4]\n      rf_keff_sig: [0, 1]\n      rf_r2: [0.40, 0.60]\n      min_eta_max_wins: [8, 10]\n      bayesian_keff_negative_frac: [0, 2]\n      practical_delta_asr_keff_iqr_pp: [0.3, 1.5]\n      diversity_capability_r: [0.55, 0.75]\n    narrative_direction: \"Core 'weakest link dominance' framing abandoned as primary claim. Reframe around three salvageable angles, still targeting EMNLP: (A) **Methodological contribution**: 'Combinatorial panel designs create massive non-independence — we demonstrate how OLS significance inflates 2-8× and provide a correction framework.' The OLS→bootstrap significance collapse itself (η_max 11→5, K_eff 8→0-1) becomes the headline finding — a cautionary tale for the growing LLM-as-judge evaluation literature. (B) **Empirical resource contribution**: largest adversarial evaluation of multi-judge panels (15 models, 455 panels, 6 attacks) with all individual-judge vulnerability profiles released. (C) **Aggregation as underexplored lever**: even if η_max vs K_eff decomposition is unreliable, the aggregation gradient (threshold R²=0.89 vs Bayesian R²=0.10) demonstrates that voting rule choice matters more than panel composition — a practically useful finding independent of the dominance question. Title candidates: 'How You Count the Votes Matters More Than Who's Voting: Aggregation Rules as the Primary Lever for LLM Evaluation Panel Security' or 'The Non-Independence Trap: Why Combinatorial Panel Evaluations Overestimate Diversity Effects.' Paper restructured: §1-2 setup + dataset description, §3 the non-independence problem (methodological core), §4 aggregation gradient (empirical core), §5 panel design recommendations (practical), §6 limitations including failed η_max dominance claim. Contribution stack inverted: methodology > aggregation > data resource > (weakened) compositional findings.\"\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":17337,"cache_read_input_tokens":11447,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":17337},"output_tokens":9,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d7891189-a4cd-4574-8ef9-841cc236a409","uuid":"faba941e-284c-4033-980e-1a0143f36df4"}
